WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
In Mac preview 0.1.7, pin a conversation in the session library.
The expanded notch shows the pinned tiles side by side.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
A working Codex subagent appears under Portfolio site.
The tile updates when the mobile layout checks pass.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
In the Mac source build, choose Two-column grid.
The tile shows that Codex is applying the selected layout.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The tile asks permission to save the gallery preview.
Approve once allows the save. Deny skips it.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
A follow-up is typed into Portfolio copy.
The arrow sends it through the open ChatGPT desktop composer.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
In development, a pinned ChatGPT tile shows the last observed reply.
A follow-up during an active turn can show Queued in ChatGPT.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Paste a screenshot and add a caption in the Codex tile.
The image and caption can be sent to the same thread.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.000
In development, pin a Claude Desktop chat or a local Claude Code session.
Hand off a chat draft or copy an attach command for the project terminal.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:58.000
End session offers to archive a Codex thread.
Stop response stops an active ChatGPT turn and keeps the conversation.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Enable Automatically show active sessions in the session library.
Working or waiting sessions appear alongside pins and leave when idle.
